  "lessons": [
    {
      "title": "Getting Started",
      "slug": "getting-started",
      "displayOrder": 1,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 555,
        "lessonOrder": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Custom Christmas stockings can become much-loved heirlooms, appreciated hostess gifts, re-usable gift wrap or money-making craft fair items.<br>In this knit-along we will explore 2 styles of socks with the patterns in multiple sizes from mini to jumbo.<br>Mix 'n Match Stitch pattern version is designed to incorporate a different stitch pattern on the top and bottom of the foot.<br>The Basic stocking is a bit easier to knit and has less finishing.<br>Options:<br>\r\n\r\nGather up the toe for an even faster project.\r\n\r\n<br>Don't like to short row?  consider shaping toes and heels with increases and decreases and neatly seam them to form the correct shape.<br>If you are new to knitting socks, try a mini to perfect your skills.  Don't mess with stitch patterns at first ... or just add some simple stripes.  Once you've \"got it\" consider adding fairisle, initarsia or isolated motifs.",
              "legacyComponentId": 6603,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Introduction",
          "slug": "introduction",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 4357,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<span class=\"handwriting\" style=\"font-size:2em\">If you are new:</span><br>\r\n Start small and gain confidence<br><span class=\"handwriting\" style=\"font-size:2em\">If you've \"been there .... done that\":</span><br>\r\nTry incorporating a new stitch pattern technique or knit a seamless stocking<br>",
              "legacyComponentId": 6604,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "exerciseAccordion",
              "sections": [
                {
                  "title": "Knit and measure an accurate swatch",
                  "bodyHtml": "No matter what you want to knit, <b>knitting a gauge swatch is NOT OPTIONAL!</b><br>Without knowing gauge:<ul>\r\n\t<li>How do you know how much yarn you need?</li>\r\n\t<li>How are you going to know if the finished item will fit?</li>\r\n\t<li>Determine if you are even going to LIKE the resulting fabric</li>\r\n\t<li>Try out the chosen stitch pattern, maybe it's too tedious... learn this BEFORE starting to knit</li>\r\n\t<li>Dress the swatch and check for shrinkage, pilling, fading</li>\r\n\t<li>Save time by knowing AHEAD if the yarn will knit easily</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n\t<img src=\"/path/images/87/measure_rows.jpg\">\r\n\t<img src=\"/path/images/87/measure_stitches.jpg\">\r\n",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/91/arrow1.png"
                },
                {
                  "title": "Decisions, Decisions, Decisions",
                  "bodyHtml": "<b><mark>Leg:</mark></b>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Ribbing, Mock Rib, Plain or stitch pattern?</li>\r\n<li>Cuff, Rolled Edge, Ribbing or ???</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<b><mark>Heel / Toe:</mark></b>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Short rows</li>\r\n<li>Decrease/Increase method</li>\r\n<li>Gathered toe???</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<b><mark>Stitch Patterns:</mark></b>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Stripes</li>\r\n<li>Fairisle</li>\r\n<li>Isolated Motif</li>\r\n<li>Intarsia</li>\r\n</ul>",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/91/arrow2.png"
                },
                {
                  "title": "Build the Knit it Now Stocking Pattern",
                  "bodyHtml": " <i class=\"fa fa-question-circle\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> <a data-vimeoid=\"402313052\" class=\"videopopup\"> Are you new to Knit it Now Patterns? </a><br><a href=\"\"><img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/91/pattern_thumb.jpg\">\r\n</a>",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/91/arrow3.png"
                },
                {
                  "title": "Follow the pattern and knit your stocking",
                  "bodyHtml": "\r\n\r\n\r\n<br>Make notes in the pattern as you go.... any time you see<br> a pencil icon <i class=\"fa fa-pencil\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> you can type.<br>Save your notes directly in your pattern.<br>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/91/notes.jpg\">\r\n",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/91/arrow4.png"
                },
                {
                  "title": "Finishing",
                  "bodyHtml": "Seaming can make or break your project ... take time to make the seams perfect!",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/91/arrow5.png"
                }
              ],
